    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Some ancestry or class selections apply a Drachiri Benefactor, such as the Draichsar ancestry, the Draich versatile heritage, or the Drachensoul manafont archetype.</p><p>@UUID[Compendium.immortal-ardor.journals.JournalEntry.HO16IW50jXn58kdN.JournalEntryPage.T8JnPSTdBowegkTJ]{Draconic Characters}</p><h2>Drachiri Benefactor</h2><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dragons are strongly influenced by their type. For verum drachiri, or true dragons, this ranges from everything to their biology, their magical influences, and their ancestral Curse of Greed. For other draconic ancestries and creatures, some of these traits are passed onto their drachenchild.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The Drachiri Benefactor table below behaves similarly to the Draconic Benefactor features in that a draconic affiliated character or creature bears the drachiri’s qualities, and even their curse. It affects your scale color, your appearance, certain capabilities and their elemental affiliations or domains, and if applicable the Curse of Greed your character experiences.</p><table border=\"1\" class=\"pf2e lost-omens\"><thead><tr style=\"text-align:right\"><th data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Benefactor</p></th><th data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Domains, Aspects and Themes</p></th><th data-colwidth=\"186\"><p>Elements &amp; Energies</p></th><th><p>Curse of Greed</p></th><th><p>Skill</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Crimson</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Grasslands and Hills, Life, Material wealth, Seasons</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"186\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Fire, Wood, Vitality, Water</p></td><td><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greed of Wealth, manifesting to rage when not sated.</p></td><td><p>Crafting</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Azure</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Seas and Oceans, Coral, Beauty, Storms</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"186\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Water, Cold, Electricity, Sonic</p></td><td><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greed of Fame, manifesting to pride when challenged.</p></td><td><p>Performance</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Verdant</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Forests and Marshes, Decay, Excellence, Primal magic</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"186\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Air, Wood, Acid, Void</p></td><td><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greed of Power, manifesting to envy when feeling inadequate.</p></td><td><p>Nature</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Ivory</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Mountains and Frost, Knowledge, Arcane magic</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"186\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Cold, Force, Air, Earth</p></td><td><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greed of Knowledge, manifesting to apathy when nothing new is learned.</p></td><td><p>Arcana</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Ebony</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Caverns and Chasms, Dominance, Magma</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"186\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Earth, Metal, Acid, Fire</p></td><td><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greed of Vengeance, manifesting to a desire for pain on oneself and others when a grudge is not repaid.</p></td><td><p>Society</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Violet</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Crystal, Light, Dreams and History, Emotions, Occult magic</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"186\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Mental, Force, Sonic, Metal</p></td><td><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Greed of Pleasure, which manifests to hedonism when indulged, and sloth when unchallenged.</p></td><td><p>Occultism</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thematically, certain drachiri-influenced territories and cultures revolve around ideas and environments listed in the Domains, Aspects and Themes column, while mechanically, they are affiliated most strongly to the elements and energies listed in that column.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">While not every draconic character is affected by the curse listed by their drachiri benefactor, some are partially influenced or have features or traits that parrot or exemplify it in some way. In this instance, this typically results in an appropriate set of Edicts and Anathemas that your character must or should abide by, associated to the respective curse. Work with your GM to create an appropriate pair for your character, based on their own or their culture’s interpretations.</p><h2>Drachiri Breath Damage, Weapon Group &amp; Saves</h2><p>Not every drachiri breath weapon is the same. There is a typical alignment between their trait with a particular style of attack, and the table below highlights the weapon group affiliated with a given trait. Some options will ask you to select a saving throw affiliated with your breath weapon when you take them, while others might ask you to choose a saving throw when you use the option.</p><table border=\"1\" class=\"pf2e lost-omens\"><thead><tr style=\"text-align:right\"><th data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Trait &amp; Weapon Group</p></th><th data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Saving Throw</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fire (Flame)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Cold (Cryo)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Electricity (Plasma)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Air (Knife)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Water (Club)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Mental (Shock)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Will</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Vitality</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Will</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Earth (Hammer)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Metal (Sword)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Reflex, Will</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Wood (Spear)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Sonic (Sonic)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Will</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Acid (Corrosive)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Force (Flail)</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Reflex</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Void</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"198\"><p>Fortitude, Will</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><span>For the purpose of damage types associated with these traits, Metal or Air correlates to slashing damage, Water or Wood correlates to piercing, and Earth correlates to bludgeoning.</span></p>",
